{"duration_api_ms":75990,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"39db2910-2137-4d10-b4f1-c3f81f17dd3e","total_cost_usd":0.13656200000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13882,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":8103,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3135},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13882,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8103,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13882,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13882},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":8103,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13882,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.13656200000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3135,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"All 20 round-2 proposals were wasted on the invalid corner (bluntness 1.25-1.35, cone 70, D around 3.36). The geometry check rejects any cone angle too small for the nose radius, and the fore cone length goes negative. At D=3.36 and cone 70, the overrun is -12.7 mm at b=1.30 and -33.7 mm at b=1.35, so the limit is near b=1.27. b=1.25 also failed a separate surrogate check (cd_fore outside its training hull). The only feasible designs sit at b=1.1-1.18, cone 68-70, D 3.2-3.3. Within that set, lower gamma gives lower heat flux and higher bondline temperature (about 264k W/m2 and 411 K at -2.2 deg, about 290k and 394 K at -3.5 deg). Peak g reaches about 11.83 at -3.5 deg and hits its 12 g limit near -3.6 deg. The mass-fraction margin shrinks as D grows (0.106 at D 3.2, 0.078 at 3.25, 0.046 at 3.3 with cone 68). This round stays inside the proven envelope and fills the front along gamma, D and mild bluntness changes.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-b86d67fded52 (D 3.2, b 1.18, cone 70, gamma -2.2): 263.6k W/m2, 411.2 K, feasible. This is the low-flux end of the front.\",\"C-51e48573fc56 (D 3.25, b 1.18, cone 70, gamma -3.5): 290.4k W/m2, 394.3 K, g margin 0.014. This is the low-temperature end.\",\"C-114b79b08144 (gamma -3.7, b 1.1, D 3.2): g 12.136, infeasible. Together with C-84c7c9af373d (g 11.68 at -3.4) this puts the g limit near gamma -3.6 deg.\",\"C-84c7c9af373d (D 3.3, cone 68): mass margin 0.0455, so D above about 3.35 risks the mass-fraction constraint.\",\"C-2317645f3652, C-f986776067bd, C-733b361d9f0d and the b=1.35 rejections: bluntness at or above 1.25 with cone 69-70 is invalid or outside the hull, so keep b at or below about 1.22.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Stagnation heating falls with nose radius, so higher bluntness and larger D help. Peak g is set mainly by gamma, and mass fraction limits D. Bondline temperature follows heat load, which is lower for a steeper, shorter pulse. Steep gamma near -3.55 to -3.6 lowers temperature while staying just under the g limit. Shallow gamma (-1.5 to -2.2) lowers peak flux and extends the front to the left. The hypervolume uses a 450 K reference, so a few kelvin of bondline temperature is worth much more than tens of thousands of W/m2. Effects of cone angle and of b between 1.18 and 1.22 are not well known from the data, so I probe them cautiously. These rely partly on prior physical knowledge, not only on the tables.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The g-versus-gamma slope is interpolated from designs with different D and b, so gamma of -3.58 to -3.6 may cross 12 g. The mass-fraction margin at D 3.34-3.36 is extrapolated. The b=1.20-1.22 points at cone 70 may fail the geometry or hull check. Effects of cone angle are essentially unobserved. Predicted fluxes and temperatures are linear interpolations and may be off by a few percent.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-51e48573fc56\",\"rationale\":\"Push gamma slightly steeper to lower temperature while keeping g under 12.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":292500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests how close to the g limit the front can be pushed.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-51e48573fc56\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly larger D lowers ballistic coefficient and heating; mass margin should stay positive.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.28,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the D benefit at near-limit g with a mass margin of about 0.06.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-51e48573fc56\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.3 with b 1.18 and cone 70 gives a lower ballistic coefficient than the front designs.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":287000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Direct D sensitivity at fixed b and cone.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-51e48573fc56\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the mass-fraction boundary with larger D and a lower b that stays geometrically safe.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.34,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the D limit set by mass fraction, which caps further improvement.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b86d67fded52\",\"rationale\":\"Extend the front toward minimum flux with a very shallow gamma.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":255000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":421,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the low-flux end of the front; temperature margin should hold.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b86d67fded52\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow gamma with slightly larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":257000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the front between -1.6 and -2.2 with a larger D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b86d67fded52\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the mid-front at b 1.18 (the front's mid points at b 1.1 have higher flux).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":277000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Interpolation point that may dominate the b=1.1 point C-a2a24d2b0ad2.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b86d67fded52\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-front with larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":282000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the gap between -2.9 and -3.5 deg with a higher-D design.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b86d67fded52\",\"rationale\":\"Small bluntness increase to 1.22 to lower nose heating; still below the b~1.27 geometry limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.22},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":258000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether b 1.22 passes the geometry and hull checks and whether it reduces flux.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-51e48573fc56\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 1.22 at the steep-gamma corner.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.22,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":284000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Same test at the low-temperature corner where it would matter most for hypervolume.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-51e48573fc56\",\"rationale\":\"Combine b 1.2 with D 3.3 near the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":284000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Combined best-guess corner within the observed envelope.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b86d67fded52\",\"rationale\":\"Larger D at shallow gamma to lower flux and temperature together.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":260000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"D sensitivity on the shallow-gamma branch.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-84c7c9af373d\",\"rationale\":\"Cone angle is unexplored; reducing it to 66 shows its effect on drag and heating. The geometry is safer at b 1.1.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":288000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Measures the cone-angle sensitivity at fixed D, b and gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-84c7c9af373d\",\"rationale\":\"A larger cone change to 62 to see the trend, with b lowered slightly to keep the fore cone length positive.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":62.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":310000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps a different region of the design space and the cone-angle trend.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a2a24d2b0ad2\",\"rationale\":\"Larger D at b 1.1 to test the mass-fraction limit with a different nose.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":286000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Mass margin at D 3.35 is uncertain; the result shows where the constraint binds.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-51e48573fc56\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller D leaves more mass margin and allows a gamma at the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.22,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":293500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the g boundary at gamma -3.6 deg.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b86d67fded52\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the mass boundary from the shallow-gamma side with D 3.36 and b 1.15.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":282000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether D 3.36 is feasible when b is reduced to 1.15.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a2a24d2b0ad2\",\"rationale\":\"Increase cone angle to the 70 limit at b 1.14 and mid gamma.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.14,\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":278000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the mid-front with a b/cone combination between the two known families.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b86d67fded52\",\"rationale\":\"Most extreme shallow gamma with b 1.2 and D 3.25 to probe the minimum-flux end.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":247000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":424,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Finds the low-flux extreme and checks the temperature limit of 450 K.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":35722,"type":"result","duration_ms":76025,"uuid":"1fc7ecf4-d14c-4ca3-8416-1cc18318be70","ttft_stream_ms":1152,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":1152,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
